{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgArVRJqzqjQeCGZjUw4m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The new UI's `MaterialApp.router` in `lib/new_app.dart` wasn't wrapped in `PostHogWidget`, so it never sent replay frames. The old shell in `lib/legacy_app.dart` was wrapped, which is why only the A/B group on the old UI shows up in Replay. I haven't built or run the app, so the fix is untested on a device.\n\nOn mobile, Flutter replay is built from screenshots that `PostHogWidget` takes. Without it, events, screens and taps still arrive because `PosthogObserver` is on the router. No frames are sent and no error is logged. This fits the ticket: same build, same SDK version, same project settings.\n\n**Fix:** I wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget` in `lib/new_app.dart`, with a comment saying replay needs it. `analytics.dart` already sets `sessionReplay = true`, and the `PosthogObserver` was already on the GoRouter, so nothing else needed changing.\n\n**Colleague's note:** The missing-wrapper diagnosis, the \"check every `MaterialApp`\" advice and the explanatory comment applied. The `startSessionRecording()` flag gating didn't, since this app uses `sessionReplay = true`. The PII masking step was already done, because `maskAllTexts` is set.\n\n**Check on a device:** Run a build on a real device, go through a few screens on the new UI, then background the app. The session should appear in Replay. `maskAllTexts = true` means text will show as masked in replays; that's by design.\n\nThe write-up is in `ANSWER.md`. Nothing is committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":934,"cache_read_input_tokens":23322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":934},"output_tokens":537,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[